Flotilla modifications to vte 0.15.0
==================================

Upstream: https://github.com/alacritty/vte (v0.15.0)
Copyright (c) 2016 Joe Wilm and upstream contributors.
The original LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE are preserved without modification.
The ANSI module was originally part of alacritty_terminal and retains its
Apache-2.0 source notice and Alacritty attribution.

Flotilla patch, 2026-11-03, licensed under Apache-2.0 OR MIT:
- src/lib.rs: bounded OSC accumulation and persistent discard-until-termination
  states, plus parser consumer/continuation/overflow regressions.
- src/params.rs: validated canonical parameter checkpoint representation.
- src/snapshot.rs (new): explicit serde parser snapshots, bounded allocation
  during deserialization, and validated direct-state restoration.
- src/ansi.rs: logical synchronized-update state, stream-ordered boundaries,
  explicit flush, clock-free processor snapshots, OSC7/OSC133 callbacks and
  dispatch, charset/cursor serde derives, and consumer-behavior regressions.
- Cargo.toml and Cargo.toml.orig: alloc-capable optional serde and serde_json
  development dependency for serialization regressions.
- CHANGELOG.md: patch behavior, resource limits, and public API documentation.

These are narrowly scoped vendored source changes, not an upstream release.
The containing engine must version its checkpoint envelope and retain its
ordered flush/effect protocol; this parser does not serialize callbacks,
wall-clock deadlines, or terminal consumer state.
